From 61be560ebf3f50d46a1935825dd900effa32c112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:41:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(host-contracts): ACL v0.4.1 backport of account
 retirement (lifecycle Core, Level 0)

Backports the Core of the Decryption Authority Lifecycle to the v0.13 line,
built from the v0.13.8 tag source (delegation expiry stays `>`):

- retireAccount() / isAccountRetired(address) and the AccountRetired event,
  with state in the dedicated ERC-7201 namespace fhevm.storage.ACLRetirement
  (0xe6ae1005...86200). Not gated by pause or deny list; one-way.
- View gating: isAllowed answers false for a retired account unless the
  caller is the FHEVMExecutor (operand-check exemption, raw persisted read);
  persistAllowed and isHandleDelegatedForUserDecryption gate the delegator,
  the delegate and the contract; getUserDecryptionDelegationExpirationDate
  returns 0.
- Grant paths: typed SenderRetired in the failure branch of allow,
  allowForDecryption and allowTransient, and as the first statement of
  delegateForUserDecryption. Never-retired callers are unaffected.
- ERC-165 supportsInterface (0x01ffc9a7, Core 0x556d2088),
  retirementStorageLocation(), and an upgrade guard in _authorizeUpgrade
  that reverts UpgradeDropsRetirement unless the new implementation
  declares Core and reports the same storage location.
- ACL v0.4.0 -> v0.4.1, REINITIALIZER_VERSION 5 -> 6, reinitializeV5().

Existing tests: two version-string assertions follow the bump, and the
owner-upgrade test now targets a Core-declaring ACL implementation, since
the guard refuses EmptyUUPSProxyACL by design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
